TEST AUTOMATION

This project for the SDET exercise. I tested https://www.saucedemo.com with
Robot Framework, Python and SeleniumLibrary, and wrote a small tool that
updates my test plan spreadsheet after each run.

Setup
You need Python 3.10+, Google Chrome and Git.

    git clone https://github.com/lloydangelotadeo/JR_QA-test.git
    cd JR_QA-test
    python -m venv venv
    venv\Scripts\activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt

    Note: I used Windows

From the project folder:

    robot -d results tests

To also update the spreadsheet:

    robot -d results --listener libraries\ScenarioSync.py:data\test_scenarios.xlsx tests

Results go to `results/` (`report.html` for the summary, `log.html` for
details and failure screenshots).

What to expect:
8 tests: 6 pass, 2 fail. The failures (SC-01, SC-02) are on purpose. They
check what the site should do, and it doesn't yet. They're tagged
`known-bug`; add `--exclude known-bug` to skip them.

Structure:
    tests/        test cases (login, checkout, smoke)
    resources/    pages/ = locators, keywords/ = reusable steps
    libraries/    ScenarioSync, my custom tool
    data/         test plan spreadsheet

Locators, steps and tests are in separate files, so if the site changes I
fix one place. The login tests use one keyword with a table of data.

Bugs I found:
- SC-01: checkout accepts a nonsense postal code like "@@@@".
- SC-02: you can finish checkout with an empty cart.

ScenarioSync
A Robot listener that matches each test to a spreadsheet row by its ID
for example, SC-03 and writes PASS/FAIL and the time after the run.
